{
  "id": "16_rover_drive_a",
  "title": "Driving Feel: Forward, Reverse & Tire Traction",
  "label": "车轮前进与倒退测试",
  "duration": 28.733333333333334,
  "voice_timing": [
    {
      "start": 0.2,
      "duration": 6.56,
      "text": "Hop into the driver's seat and tap the accelerator! We run a low-speed crawl forward and backward at ground level to examine tire rotation.",
      "source": "modules/16_rover_drive_a/audio/87e98ccca970c8052900.wav"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.01,
      "duration": 7.76,
      "text": "Relative to the chassis, the contact patch of each tire must sweep backward against the terrain as the vehicle drives forward, reversing smoothly when backing up.",
      "source": "modules/16_rover_drive_a/audio/178745e04b51ad6431c5.wav"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.02,
      "duration": 13.36,
      "text": "The wide treads grip the grass naturally. Forward acceleration, braking, and reverse motion all synchronize with satisfying mechanical weight. If you ever want to tweak torque or gearing, a single message to your agent updates the script instantly.",
      "source": "modules/16_rover_drive_a/audio/102d46f37f56a41b5662.wav"
    }
  ],
